<section class="sg-sec" id="inspired"><h2>What it inspired</h2><ul class="sg-chain"><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Swedish translation, presumably by Olaus Petri</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1536</span><span class="sg-chain-h">translation</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Myles Coverdale's English version</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1539</span><span class="sg-chain-h">translation</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Frederick H. Hedge's English version</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1853</span><span class="sg-chain-h">translation</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Thomas Carlyle's English version</span><span class="sg-chain-h">translation</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Ein feste Burg ist unser Gott, organ chorale BWV 720 (J. S. Bach)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">adapted as</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Ein feste Burg ist unser Gott, cantata BWV 80 (J. S. Bach)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">adapted as</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Donnerode (Georg Philipp Telemann)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">quoted in</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Solomon (George Frideric Handel)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">quoted in</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Symphony No. 5 &quot;Reformation&quot;, Op. 107 (Felix Mendelssohn)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1830</span><span class="sg-chain-h">same melody (theme of the finale)</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Les Huguenots (Giacomo Meyerbeer)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1836</span><span class="sg-chain-h">quoted in</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Impromptu for pedal piano, Op. 69 (Charles-Valentin Alkan)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1866</span><span class="sg-chain-h">adapted as</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Kaisermarsch (Richard Wagner)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1871</span><span class="sg-chain-h">quoted in</span></li></ul></section>
<section class="sg-sec" id="inspired-by"><h2>What it drew on</h2><ul class="sg-chain"><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Psalm 46</span><span class="sg-chain-h">paraphrase of its opening</span></li></ul></section>
